{"name":"Bran","hex":"#a9704c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bran","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bran"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bran","blocks":[{"text":"Bran, also known as miller's bran, is the component of a cereal grain consisting of the outer hard layers – the combined aleurone and pericarp – surrounding the endosperm. Corn (maize) bran also includes the pedicel. Along with the germ, it is an integral part of whole grains, and is often produced as a byproduct of milling in the production of refined grains. Bran is very nutritious, but is difficult to digest due to its high fiber content; its high fat content also reduces its shelf life as the oils/fats are prone to becoming rancid. As such, it is typically removed from whole grain during the refining process – e.g. in processing wheat grain into white flour, or refining brown rice into white rice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Wheat_bran_structure.gif/330px-Wheat_bran_structure.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bran","wikidata":"Q188672"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Rice_bran.jpg/500px-Rice_bran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Rice_bran.jpg/1280px-Rice_bran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Rice_bran.jpg/500px-Rice_bran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rice bran","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARice_bran.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/WheatBran.jpg/500px-WheatBran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb